metadata.description:
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Moves items, markers and regions starting at or after the time selection start. One bar is intentionally four quarter notes (4/4), as in the original script. Automation and tempo markers are not moved. Back up your project first.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Generate passing chords between start and target chords, with automatic, ascending-step and descending-cycle modes, voicing previews and pagination. Requires REAPER with Lua ReaScript support and the ReaImGui extension (available through ReaPack). SWS is optional, for opening chord-reference URLs. Audition uses the virtual MIDI keyboard queue: enable track monitoring and select All MIDI inputs or Virtual MIDI keyboard as the track input.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Quantize selected MIDI items for notation using the native gfx options panel. Supports polyphonic/monophonic cleanup and optional copies on new tracks. Normalizes retained velocities to 100; removes CC-class events except pitch bend. Text, lyrics and SysEx are preserved. No extensions required.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Revoice selected notes independently in each editable MIDI-editor take. Native gfx chord panel, external-note strategies and collision-safe additions. REAPER 6/7, Lua 5.3+. No SWS/ReaPack dependencies.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 First run: opens the floating window of the first active effect on the selected track, preferring an instrument. Running it again from the same shortcut closes the open effect windows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Uses only native REAPER actions, so no extension is required.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Closing note: TrackFX_Show(..., 0) hides the FX chain window rather than the floating window, so floating windows must be closed with 2.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Independent implementation using native REAPER APIs; no SWS required. Finds the first instrument on each selected track, then its nearest parent, then searches send destinations breadth-first (including their parents). Send traversal handles cycles. Shared instruments are processed once. If any resolved window is closed, show all; otherwise close all. This changes floating windows only, not FX bypass, offline state or routing.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Reads the instrument of every selected track and writes a "Sound:" line into the track note. Tracks that already carry the same line are left untouched.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Uses only native REAPER actions, so no extension is required.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Selected tracks with FX are shown in both TCP and mixer, with FX online. Unselected tracks with all FX offline are hidden. Tracks without FX are unchanged.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Independent native REAPER gfx calculator. No FX, SWS, ReaImGui or other dependencies. Beats are quarter-note beats (4 beats = one 4/4 bar); duration is in seconds. Convert beats + seconds to BPM, or beats + BPM to seconds. Tap with the mouse or Space. Tap intervals below 0.10 seconds are ignored; a gap over 3 seconds starts a new sequence. Average the latest 16 intervals. Space uses physical key-down edges to avoid keyboard auto-repeat taps. This utility never changes project tempo, transport, selection or media.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER with the ReaImGui extension (available through ReaPack).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Usage:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Select a time range in the arrange view. Without a time selection the range of the selected media item is used.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Click a preset button. The button shows "English (Chinese)" while only the English part is written into the Region.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Right click a preset button to edit or delete it, and use the add button to create a new preset.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Clicking a preset again at the same position renames and recolours the existing Region instead of stacking a duplicate.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Repeating sections are numbered automatically as Verse 1, Verse 2 and so on. Each preset decides on its own whether it takes part in the numbering, so Intro and Outro stay unnumbered by default.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER with the ReaImGui extension (available through ReaPack).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Renames the selected tracks from a preset list and stores the presets in the project state. Presets show an English name with a Chinese reference, while the written track name keeps the plain underscore form.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The two columns can be resized by dragging the divider.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Button widths follow the length of their text.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Preset search, collapsible categories, and multi select, select all, invert and batch delete with a confirmation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Automatic numbering for repeated names, and the next track is selected after applying a preset.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab A world instrument library window that can add its entries to the preset list in one click.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Presets can be taken from the selected track, and colours are picked with a colour picker.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER with ReaImGui 0.10+ (install/update via ReaPack). Reading mode already centers each visual line and uses an opaque black background with white text; selection, copying and Region follow are preserved. FangSong is optional; portable sans-serif fallback may lack CJK glyph coverage. Edits update project notes, not the project file: save the project in REAPER. Backups/recovery use hex-encoded persistent ExtState (not encrypted). Recovery copies drafts to the clipboard; legacy recovery remains readable. Korean and Tibetan glyphs use optional extra fonts, selected per character; missing font files fall back to the base font.\par}
}

version.changelog:
v5.1.2: Guard optional font loading; verify note writes before marking synced;
preserve multiline backup/recovery data using single-line hex ExtState.
Existing centered, opaque high-contrast reader and follow behavior unchanged.

metadata.description:
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Manage persistent URL bookmarks from a mouse-position popup menu. Supports opening, adding, renaming, editing URLs, deleting, and reordering. Opening requires SWS CF_ShellExecute; only HTTP(S) and file URLs are allowed. File URLs use the system handler and must only point to trusted files.\par}
}
